use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback was denied by a human reviewer, who says the problem is in `payments-worker`, not `payments-api`. The incident call timed out, so I don't know yet whether it was created. I'll look at `payments-worker` before doing anything else.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Sug2HPEUFyZKBq2SJXcweJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01KGrfDCZA9njHPq9bZYDgsr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013tRNqo3YnVCMQunDothD4w", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "`payments-worker` v3.4.0 is unhealthy (error rate 0.18), and v3.3.0 is its most recent healthy production release. This matches the reviewer's note, so I'll roll `payments-worker` back to v3.3.0 and open the SEV2 incident against it. The earlier incident attempt doesn't appear in the incident list, so I'm using a new idempotency key.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_014MrYUrQjY6gL8ZgQcWerR2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01EZdTWs7CG1K1adv99wFW43", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker errors following v3.4.0 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "payments-worker v3.4.0 deployed this morning to us-east, us-west, eu-west and is unhealthy (error rate 0.18). Rolled back to last healthy production release v3.3.0. payments-api was flagged in an earlier attempt but the reviewer identified payments-worker as the source; payments-api was not changed.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01PaaL6ZmR3vkQL8hhHaN3ks", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The payments errors came from `payments-worker`, not `payments-api`. I rolled `payments-worker` back to v3.3.0, and it is now healthy in all three regions (error rate 0.002). I opened SEV2 incident INC-0002, which paged on-call.\n\n- **First attempt, `payments-api`:** I rolled it back to v5.0.0 and opened an incident, but the reviewer denied the rollback and said the problem was in `payments-worker`. `payments-api` was not changed. Its status shows v5.1.0 degraded at 0.18 error rate, though. That may just be a side effect of the same incident, but it's worth checking.\n- **Incident timeout:** The first incident request timed out and I couldn't confirm whether it was created. `list_incidents` showed no incident at that point, so I opened INC-0002 for `payments-worker`. If an incident for `payments-api` appears later, it's a duplicate and should be closed.\n- **Rollback:** `payments-worker` v3.4.0 was unhealthy (0.18 error rate). I rolled it back to v3.3.0, its most recent healthy production release. A human reviewer approved the rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}